{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Before we scope the build, the most load-bearing decision is what we actually stand up first. This repo is empty, so the very first mission isn't the Mint clone — it's the FOUNDATION: a booting skeleton, a real test runner a human can watch run, and one thin slice proving they're wired together. Every feature you named (Plaid sync, budgets, charts, mobile app, CSV import, recurring-bill detection, multi-currency, household mode) gets recorded in the vision doc and filed as its own mission right after. For the foundation stack, I'd recommend **Vite + React + TypeScript + Vitest** — it boots a web UI fast, Vitest gives you a watchable test run, and it's a natural base for the budgets-and-charts personal-finance app you're describing. Does a TypeScript web app sound right, or were you picturing something else (e.g. mobile-first native, or a Python/backend-first build)?","choices":["Vite + React + TypeScript + Vitest (recommended)","Mobile-first native (e.g. React Native / Expo)","Backend-first (e.g. Python/FastAPI or Node API)","Something else"],"recommended":"Vite + React + TypeScript + Vitest"},"prd":"# Mission: Foundation skeleton for personal-finance app\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up a booting web skeleton with a watchable test runner and one thin vertical slice proving both are wired together.\n\n_(PRD in progress — foundation stack and proving slice still being confirmed with the captain.)_"}

